=== USER QUERY
Follow-up visit, room 214B. Chief complaint: shortness of breath on exertion for 3 days.
Code status: full code. Meds: lisinopril 10 mg daily, metformin 500 mg twice daily; aspirin stopped last week.
Social: former smoker, quit 10 years ago, lives alone, no alcohol. Family history: father had an MI at 60.
BP 148/92 sitting, repeat 142/88. Pain 3/10 in the left knee. Temp 99.1.
ENMT: oral mucosa moist, no pharyngeal erythema. Labs: HbA1c 7.8, potassium 4.1.
Assessment: 1) hypertension, not at goal - increase lisinopril to 20 mg daily. 2) type 2 diabetes - continue metformin.
Follow up in 2 weeks.
